Here are ten sentences that end in the word "apple":

1. For lunch today, I packed a sandwich and an apple.
2. My grandmother's famous pie recipe calls for one large Granny Smith apple.
3. The teacher smiled when the student placed on her desk a shiny red apple.
4. After biting into the fruit, I discovered a worm living inside my apple.
5. Isaac Newton supposedly discovered gravity after being hit on the head by a falling apple.
6. Of all the fruits in the orchard, my favorite has always been the apple.
7. The horse gently took the treat from my outstretched hand—a crisp, juicy apple.
8. In the fairy tale, the evil queen disguised herself and offered Snow White a poisoned apple.
9. When making cider, you'll get the best flavor from a tart rather than a sweet apple.
10. Nothing says autumn quite like the first bite of a freshly picked apple. [end of text]


